# upstream/80-walk-iterative: every walk keeps its place on an explicit
# stack, so its native depth does not grow with the IR's nesting, and the
# tools keep a small stack. Each kind of walk (both orders, every
# iterator, regions, blocks, by stage, interrupted and skipped) over
# operations nested 10,000 deep, on a thread whose stack is 256 KiB, visits
# what the recursion visited (walk.cpp). The nesting is built in memory:
# mlir-opt's parser recurses on the same depth through each operation's
# parse hook, so through mlir-opt the walk is never seen alone.
# Building a program against MLIR's libraries takes longer than a step.
step_limit=180
. "$IDRIS_MLIR_ROOT/harness/testutils.sh"
mlir_check "walk: every kind over 10,000 nested operations on a 256 KiB stack" "$here/walk.cpp" 10000
